@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Create Admission Class (Valid)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Class 6 - Morning Shift",
  "totalSeats": 120
}

### 3. Create Admission Class (Invalid - Empty name & 0 seats)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "totalSeats": 0
}

### 4. Get All Admission Classes (Includes calculated held, confirmed, available seats)
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes
Accept: application/json

### 5. Get Admission Class by ID (Replace with a valid UUID from step 2 or 4)
# Example UUID:
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/641cf783-6881-4ca1-b400-a6b9b00a9918
Accept: application/json

### 6. Get Non-existent Admission Class (404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

### ===========================================================================
### Phase 3: Admission Hold System Endpoints
### ===========================================================================

### 7. Create Admission Hold (Valid - Endpoint A)
# Replace {classId} with a valid UUID from step 2 or step 4
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/d454f25f-652e-47b1-921d-179f38362285/holds
X-Student-Id: 20152691234567890
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 8. Create Admission Hold (Invalid - Missing X-Student-Id Header -> 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/d454f25f-652e-47b1-921d-179f38362285/holds
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 9. Create Admission Hold (Invalid - Less than 17 digits -> 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/d454f25f-652e-47b1-921d-179f38362285/holds
X-Student-Id: 12345
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 10. Create Admission Hold (Non-existent class -> 404 Not Found)
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/holds
X-Student-Id: 20152691234567890
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 11. Get Hold Details by ID (Endpoint B)
# Replace {holdId} with the UUID returned from step 7
GET {{baseUrl}}/holds/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

### 12. Get Non-existent Hold (404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/holds/ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff
Accept: application/json

### ===========================================================================
### Phase 4: Hold Lifecycle Endpoints
### ===========================================================================

### 13. Confirm a Hold (POST /holds/{holdId}/confirm -> 200 OK)
# Replace {holdId} with the UUID returned from step 7
POST {{baseUrl}}/holds/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/confirm
X-Student-Id: 20152691234567890

### 14. Confirm a Hold (Missing X-Student-Id -> 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/holds/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/confirm

### 15. Confirm an Expired Hold (409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/holds/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/confirm
X-Student-Id: 20152691234567890

### 16. Cancel a Hold (DELETE /holds/{holdId} -> 204 No Content)
# Replace {holdId} with the UUID returned from step 7
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/holds/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Student-Id: 20152691234567890

### 17. Cancel a Confirmed Hold (409 Conflict)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/holds/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Student-Id: 20152691234567890

### 18. Get My Applications (GET /me/holds -> 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/holds
X-Student-Id: 20152691234567890
Accept: application/json

### 19. Get My Applications (Missing X-Student-Id -> 400 Bad Request)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/holds
Accept: application/json

### 20. Get My Applications (Unknown student -> 200 OK with empty array)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/holds
X-Student-Id: 99999999999999999
Accept: application/json
